B.b6R=new A.dc("Lesson 1 \u2014 Actions Are by Intentions","The Prophet \ufdfa said: actions are only by intentions, and every person shall have only what they intended. Migration for Allah and His Messenger is for Allah; migration for worldly gain or marriage is for that. This hadith is one third of knowledge (as the scholars counted) because intention decides the value of everything that follows it.","Check the why before the what \u2014 one intention today, named.",1,null)
B.b7a=new A.dc("Lesson 2 \u2014 The Core of the Matter","Islam is built on five: the testimony that none is worthy of worship but Allah and Muhammad is His Messenger, establishing prayer, giving zakat, fasting Ramadan, and Hajj to the House for whoever can make the way. The Prophet \ufdfa said this to Jibril when he came as a man to teach the companions \u2014 the questions were for you.","Hold the five pillars daily; they are the frame of everything else.",3,null)
B.b6Z=new A.dc("Lesson 3 \u2014 The Levels of the Deen","Jibril asked about Islam, then Iman, then Ihsan. Islam is the five pillars. Iman is belief in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, the Last Day, and decree \u2014 good and bad. Ihsan is to worship Allah as though you see Him \u2014 and though you do not see Him, He sees you. The deen has a body, a heart, and a beauty.","Practice one act of ihsan today: do something as if He is watching \u2014 He is.",2,null)
B.b6Q=new A.dc("Lesson 4 \u2014 Your Time of Life","The Prophet \ufdfa said: you are in the evening of one day and the morning of the next \u2014 your health before your sickness, your wealth before your poverty, your life before your death, and your free time before your busyness. Five before five, none of which return once gone.","Name one of the five-before-five you still hold; spend it today.",null,null)
B.b6J=new A.dc("Lesson 5 \u2014 The Allowed and the Forbidden Are Clear","What is lawful is clear and what is unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters unknown to many. Whoever guards the doubtful has protected their religion and honor. Leave what makes you doubt for what does not.","When a choice feels gray, choose the side your heart rests on.",6,null)
B.b74=new A.dc("Lesson 6 \u2014 The Muslim Is the One Whom People Are Safe From","The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. And the emigrant is the one who emigrates from what Allah has forbidden. The Prophet \ufdfa described the best of people as those whose goodness is hoped and whose harm is safe \u2014 safety is a character, not just a status.","Be someone whose hand and word people do not fear today.",null,"Bukhari 10")
B.b6V=new A.dc("Lesson 7 \u2014 Religion Is Sincere Counsel","The Prophet \ufdfa said: the religion is sincere counsel. We asked: to whom? He said: to Allah, His Book, His Messenger, the leaders of the Muslims, and their common people. Counsel is not flattery \u2014 it is wanting good for the one you advise.","Give one sincere piece of advice today, gently, to someone who needs it.",7,null)
B.b72=new A.dc("Lesson 8 \u2014 The Sanctity of a Muslim","Allah has made sacred the blood, wealth, and honor of every Muslim to every other Muslim. The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim \u2014 he does not wrong him, forsake him, or despise him. Whoever fulfills the rights of his brother, Allah will fulfill his.","Guard one Muslim\u2019s honor today \u2014 in speech, in silence, in a message.",35,null)
B.b70=new A.dc("Lesson 9 \u2014 Avoid What Is Doubtful","The halal is clear and the haram is clear, and between them are doubtful matters unknown to many. Whoever guards the doubtful has protected his religion and his honor. And in the body is a morsel \u2014 if it is sound the whole body is sound, and if it is corrupt the whole body is corrupt. Indeed it is the heart. The stomach's halal is the heart's halal \u2014 they rise and fall together.","Run one purchase through the doubt test this week \u2014 if it feels gray, choose the side that lets you sleep.",6,null)
B.b71=new A.dc("Lesson 10 \u2014 Leave What Does Not Concern You","Part of the excellence of a person's Islam is leaving what does not concern him. The scroll of the day is finite; every unnecessary glance, word, and scroll is a withdrawal from it. The Prophet \ufdfa measured the believer's Islam by subtraction as much as addition.","Audit one hour of your week \u2014 what did not concern you? Release it and keep the difference.",12,null)
B.b7b=new A.dc("Lesson 11 \u2014 Love for Your Brother","None of you truly believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself. This hadith is the social constitution of the ummah in one sentence \u2014 envy dies where it is practiced, and the heart learns to celebrate another's blessing as if it were its own.","When good news reaches someone this week, say alhamdulillah for them before your own heart has time to compare.",13,null)
B.b6K=new A.dc("Lesson 12 \u2014 Honoring the Guest","Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. Three days and nights of hosting, then the reward is in what was given \u2014 the guest's comfort is the host's worship, and the three-day limit is the mercy that makes hospitality sustainable.","Host or serve one guest this month \u2014 a meal, a visit, even a good word at the door.",15,null)
B.b6C=new A.dc("Lesson 13 \u2014 The Right of the Neighbor","Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor. The angel Jibril kept advising the Prophet \ufdfa about the neighbor until he thought he would make him an heir. The neighbor is the person you did not choose \u2014 which makes the kindness worth more, not less.","Do one unasked kindness for a neighbor this week \u2014 take in a package, shovel a path, ask how they are.",15,null)
B.b6P=new A.dc("Lesson 14 \u2014 The Sanctity of the Muslim","Allah has made sacred the blood, wealth, and honor of every Muslim to every other Muslim. To backbite a Muslim is to eat his flesh (49:12) \u2014 and the hadith extends the sanctity to the one who is absent: mention your brother as you would have him mention you.","Guard one Muslim's absence this week \u2014 correct the story, change the subject, or stay silent.",35,null)
B.b76=new A.dc("Lesson 15 \u2014 The Signs of the Hypocrite","Three are the signs of the hypocrite, even if he fasts and prays: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks, and when he is trusted he betrays. The Prophet \ufdfa did not say these sins eject a person from Islam \u2014 he said they are the smell of hypocrisy, and the believer checks his own breath.","Check your own three signs this week \u2014 one promise you made and have not kept. Keep it.",null,"Bukhari 33")
B.b6Y=new A.dc("Lesson 16 \u2014 Anger: Change Your Posture","Anger inflames the heart, and the Prophet \ufdfa gave practical cures. If one of you becomes angry while standing, let him sit; if the anger goes, good, and if not, let him lie down (Abu Dawud 4782). Seeking refuge in Allah from Satan calms it too (Bukhari 3282). The body is the first battlefield.","Ninety seconds: next time anger rises, sit down and stay silent for ninety seconds before speaking.",null,"Abu Dawud 4782; Bukhari 3282")
B.b6N=new A.dc("Lesson 17 \u2014 The Blessing of Provision","If you were to rely upon Allah as He deserves to be relied upon, He would provide you as He provides the birds \u2014 they leave hungry in the morning and return full. Tawakkul is not passivity; it is the bird's departure \u2014 the wings still move, but the rizq is not the bird's to manage.","Name one provision you are anxious about. Plan, then release \u2014 go out hungry in the morning.",null,"Tirmidhi 2344")
B.b6I=new A.dc("Lesson 18 \u2014 The Religion Is Sincere Counsel","The religion is sincere counsel \u2014 to Allah, His Book, His Messenger, the leaders of the Muslims, and their common people. Counsel to Allah is to oppose rivals to Him; counsel to the leaders is to correct them honestly, not flatter them; counsel to the common people is the everyday kindness.","Give one sincere counsel this week \u2014 to a leader gently, to a friend honestly, to a stranger kindly.",7,null)
B.b6M=new A.dc("Lesson 19 \u2014 The Muslim Is Safe","The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. And the emigrant is the one who emigrates from what Allah has forbidden. Safety is not the absence of power \u2014 it is the decision, made daily, not to use it.","Audit one relationship: do they feel safe from your tongue and hand? Repair the one that does not.",null,null)
B.b7_=new A.dc("Lesson 20 \u2014 The Lawful and the Unlawful","Allah is pure and accepts only what is pure. Allah has commanded the believers what He commanded the messengers: eat of the good things and act righteously. The morsel of haram blocks the dua like a locked door \u2014 the stomach's halal is the first condition of the heart's acceptance.","Run one income source through the purity test this week \u2014 even small. Clean the morsel.",10,null)
B.b6W=new A.dc("Lesson 21 \u2014 Cleanliness of Character","Purity is half of faith. And the believer is not one who taunts, curses, speaks obscenely, or speaks abusively. The tongue's cleanliness is the body's cleanliness \u2014 and the one who guards both has guarded half the deen before a single prayer is prayed.","Clean one word from your vocabulary this week \u2014 replace it with a better one, starting today.",23,null)
B.b6H=new A.dc("Lesson 22 \u2014 Lowering the Wing of Humility","Allah has revealed to me that you should humble yourselves until no one boasts over another and no one transgresses against another (Muslim 2865). Humility is a character you practise one conversation at a time.","Lower your voice and your shoulder in one interaction today \u2014 let the other person walk taller.",null,"Muslim 2865")
B.b77=new A.dc("Lesson 23 \u2014 The Best of the Best","The best among you are those who learn the Quran and teach it. And the best of you in the days of ignorance are the best in Islam, if they understand. Knowledge is the ladder \u2014 and the one who climbs it and then holds it for others is the highest of all.","Learn one verse or hadith this week well enough to teach it \u2014 then teach it to one person.",null,"Bukhari 5027")
B.b7e=new A.dc("Lesson 24 \u2014 Guarding the Tongue","Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent. And whoever guarantees me what is between his jaws and what is between his legs, I will guarantee Paradise for him. The tongue is the easiest gate to open and the hardest to close \u2014 and its spoils fill more graves than any sword.","One day this week: speak only good or stay silent. Choose the day; mark it; then keep the gate.",15,null)
B.b6E=new A.dc("Lesson 25 \u2014 The Righteousness That Matters","Righteousness is not that you turn your faces toward the east or the west \u2014 but righteousness is in the one who believes in Allah, gives wealth, establishes prayer, fulfills covenants, and is patient in hardship (2:177). The direction matters; the character matters more.","Check one covenant you made \u2014 a promise, a contract, a vow. Fulfill it this week, on time.",null,"Qur'an 2:177 (a verse, not a hadith)")
B.b6F=new A.dc("Lesson 26 \u2014 The Obligation of Brotherly Love","None of you truly believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself \u2014 the same hadith as lesson 11, here read as a matter for the whole ummah. Unity is not a slogan; it is a daily practice of wanting good for the one next to you.","Make one dua today for a brother or sister you have never met \u2014 by description, not by name.",13,null)
B.b75=new A.dc("Lesson 27 \u2014 The Law of Brotherhood","The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim \u2014 he does not wrong him, forsake him, or despise him. And whoever fulfills the needs of his brother, Allah fulfills his needs. The ummah is one body: when one limb aches, the whole body responds with fever and wakefulness.","Fulfil one need of one Muslim this week \u2014 a ride, a reference, a listening ear. Then ask for nothing.",35,null)
B.b7c=new A.dc("Lesson 28 \u2014 The Evil of Oppression","Allah says: My servants, I have forbidden oppression for Myself and made it forbidden among you, so do not oppress one another. Oppression will be darkness on the Day of Judgment \u2014 even the small oppressions: the short measure, the unpaid debt, the harsh word to the powerless.","Right one small wrong this week \u2014 a debt, a measure, a harsh word remembered. Pay it back.",24,null)
B.b6X=new A.dc("Lesson 29 \u2014 The Sanctity of the Blood","The blood, wealth, and honor of a Muslim are sacred to every Muslim \u2014 like the sanctity of this day, in this month, in this city. The Prophet \ufdfa said this standing at Arafat, on the day of the Farewell Sermon \u2014 the three sanctities were the last constitution he gave.","Honor one Muslim's honor this week \u2014 defend the absent, cover the fault, speak the good word.",null,"Bukhari 67")
B.b6S=new A.dc("Lesson 30 \u2014 The Rights of the Muslim","The Prophet \ufdfa said: five are the rights of a Muslim over a Muslim \u2014 returning the greeting, visiting the sick, following the funeral, accepting an invitation, and replying to a sneeze (Muslim 2162). Five doors that keep the ummah's house standing.","Practice one of the five this week \u2014 the one you most often skip. Just one, done fully.",null,"Muslim 2162")
B.b6G=new A.dc("Lesson 31 \u2014 The Brotherhood of Faith","The believers are but brothers, so make peace between your brothers and fear Allah that you may receive mercy (49:10). The Prophet \ufdfa said: the believers are like a structure, one part strengthening another \u2014 the hand holds the wall because the wall holds the hand.","Make peace between two people this month \u2014 even by a word, even by a smile, even by leaving.",null,"Qur'an 49:10; Bukhari 481")
B.b6D=new A.dc("Lesson 32 \u2014 No Harm and No Reciprocating Harm","There is no harm and no reciprocating harm. This principle governs traffic, trade, tenancy, and every human contract: you may not harm, and you may not answer harm with harm. The Muslim's transaction is clean on both sides of the counter.","Audit one exchange this week \u2014 did both sides leave unharmed? If not, be the one who repairs it.",32,null)
B.b73=new A.dc("Lesson 33 \u2014 The Two-Faced","The Prophet \ufdfa said that among the worst of people on the Day of Judgment is the two-faced one, who comes to these with one face and to those with another (Bukhari 6058). The believer's face is the same at the door and behind the door.","Check your two faces this week \u2014 the one at work and the one at home. Bring them closer.",null,"Bukhari 6058")
B.b6T=new A.dc("Lesson 34 \u2014 The Value of This World","Compared to the Hereafter, this world is like what comes back when one of you dips his finger in the sea \u2014 let him see what returns (Muslim 2858). And the son of Adam says 'my wealth, my wealth' \u2014 but only what he ate and consumed, or wore and wore out, or gave in charity and sent ahead is truly his (Muslim 2958).","Dip the finger: what did you send ahead this month? Name it; then add one item to the list.",null,"Muslim 2858; Muslim 2958")
B.b6U=new A.dc("Lesson 35 \u2014 The Good Word","The good word and the forgiving word are better than charity followed by harm (2:263). And speak to people kindly \u2014 the Prophet \ufdfa was not crude, loud, or foul-mouthed. The word that forgives is the word that builds; the word that shames is the word that burns.","Speak one forgiving word this week \u2014 to the one who owes you, wronged you, or forgot you.",null,"Qur'an 2:263")
B.b6L=new A.dc("Lesson 36 \u2014 The Seven Under the Shade","Seven whom Allah will shade on the Day there is no shade but His: the just ruler, the youth who grew up in worship, the man whose heart is attached to the masjid, two who love each other for Allah, the one who weeps alone, the one who gives so the left hand does not know, and the one who remembers Allah alone until the eyes overflow.","You are young now. Pick one of the seven and start building it this month \u2014 the shade is real.",null,"Bukhari 660")
B.b79=new A.dc("Lesson 37 \u2014 Pardon, and Allah's Love","Allah loves the doers of good \u2014 those who restrain their anger and pardon people (3:134) \u2014 and the servants of the Most Merciful are those who walk gently, and when the ignorant address them, say words of peace (25:63). The measure of forgiveness is the size of the wrong. To pardon is to be loved.","Pardon one debt this week \u2014 of money, of words, of attention. Let it go before they ask.",null,"Qur'an 3:134; 25:63")
B.b7d=new A.dc("Lesson 38 \u2014 The Reward of Patience","Those who are patient will be given their reward without account (39:10). No scale, no measure \u2014 the reward of sabr is weighed by the One who promised, not by the one who endured. Whatever you are carrying that no one sees \u2014 it is seen, and it is not measured.","Carry one thing one more day without complaining \u2014 and tell no one. Let the account stay with Allah.",null,"Qur'an 39:10")
B.b6O=new A.dc("Lesson 39 \u2014 The Best Charity","The best charity is that given when you are healthy and greedy, fearing poverty and hoping for wealth. The Prophet \ufdfa said: do not delay until you are at the door saying 'this is for so-and-so and that is for so-and-so' \u2014 when it is already taken from your hand.","Give one sadaqah this week before you feel ready \u2014 while the greed is still alive in your hand.",null,"Bukhari 1419")
B.b78=new A.dc("Lesson 40 \u2014 Be in This World as a Stranger","Be in this world as a stranger or a traveler \u2014 and count yourself among the dead. The Prophet \ufdfa said: I have nothing to do with the world; I am like a rider who takes shade under a tree, then leaves it and moves on. The traveler does not unpack; the stranger does not renovate.","Live as a traveler this week \u2014 use the world, thank for it, and keep the luggage light. One luxury released.",40,null)
